<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip the Arab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 204–249</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Marcus Julius Philippus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip the Arab was Roman emperor from 244 to 249, born in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. He made peace with the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-i">Shapur I</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-iii">Gordian III</a>, fought the Carpi on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, and in 248 celebrated the thousandth anniversary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He was killed in 249 in battle against his general Decius, who succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-the-arab.jpg" alt="Philip the Arab" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergey Sosnovskiy from Saint-Petersburg, Russia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Philip_the_Arab._Saint-Petersburg,_The_State_Hermitage_Museum_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
